.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH cattail 1  "cattail 0.1.0" 
.SH NAME
cattail \- Tail multiple files and glob patterns
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBcattail\fR [\fB\-n\fR|\fB\-\-lines\fR] [\fB\-\-interval\-ms\fR] [\fB\-\-prefix\fR] [\fB\-\-since\-now\fR] [\fB\-\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIPATH|GLOB\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
cattail resolves literal paths and glob patterns at startup, prints a backlog from each file, then follows appended lines live with a stable source prefix. It also watches for newly created files that match startup globs and attaches them automatically.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-n\fR, \fB\-\-lines\fR \fI<N>\fR [default: 50]
Number of backlog lines to print per startup\-resolved file
.TP
\fB\-\-interval\-ms\fR \fI<MS>\fR [default: 200]
Polling interval in milliseconds for recovery scans and file reopen checks
.TP
\fB\-\-prefix\fR \fI<PREFIX>\fR [default: basename]
How to label each output line
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
basename
.IP \(bu 2
relative
.IP \(bu 2
full
.RE
.TP
\fB\-\-since\-now\fR
Skip the backlog and only emit lines appended after startup
.TP
\fB\-\-color\fR \fI<COLOR>\fR [default: auto]
Colorize line prefixes when writing to an interactive terminal
.br

.br
\fIPossible values:\fR
.RS 14
.IP \(bu 2
auto
.IP \(bu 2
always
.IP \(bu 2
never
.RE
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.TP
<\fIPATH|GLOB\fR>
One or more file paths or glob patterns
.SH EXTRA
Examples:
  cattail /var/log/syslog /var/log/auth.log
  cattail \-n 100 \*(Aq/var/log/*.log\*(Aq
  cattail \-\-since\-now \-\-prefix relative \*(Aq/var/log/*.log\*(Aq
.SH VERSION
v0.1.0
